# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind the fourth arm (4_after_audit) of
# output/evaluation/fleurs_multilingual_summary.json: Whisper Large v3 on the
# whole FLEURS test split of six languages, scored raw and through the full
# post-processing (pipeline_full), one language per array task.
#
# Array job 8917984 (au_ml), account educ-lift, six tasks submitted on
# 2026-09-27 and run on 2026-09-28, at code 6f9bf56 with a clean tree, as
# every task's environment record and every summary's run_metadata say. The
# records are in environment/au_ml_8917984_<task>.txt beside the original's
# results on ARC, and they name the card each task ran on:
#   task 0  fr_fr   french   NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3   htc-g060
#   task 1  de_de   german   NVIDIA A100-PCIE-40GB   htc-g015
#   task 2  es_419  spanish  NVIDIA L40S             htc-g081
#   task 3  it_it   italian  NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3   htc-g060
#   task 4  nl_nl   dutch    NVIDIA L40S             htc-g081
#   task 5  pl_pl   polish   NVIDIA L40S             htc-g064
# A five-utterance pre-flight of task 0, job 8917983 (pf_ml, WER_ML_LIMIT=5,
# into audit2026/preflight_ml), ran just before it.
#
# The script asks for any GPU. In the summary's first three arms, two runs
# of a language on cards of one architecture wrote identical raw
# summaries, while runs on different architectures differed on up to four
# utterances (its finding.control). The commands below therefore ask for
# the card type each task ran on: for tasks 0 and 3 the h100 type with the
# nvlink feature, which among the h100 nodes only htc-g059 and htc-g060
# have, for task 1 the a100 type (htc-g015 to htc-g018, A100 cards with
# 40 GB), and for tasks 2, 4 and 5 the l40s type.
#
# WER_ML_MODEL and WER_ML_CONDITIONS below are the script's defaults at
# 6f9bf56, written out so that a later change of a default cannot change
# what this record reproduces. WER_ML_LIMIT is set empty, which the script
# reads as the whole split, so that a value left in the calling shell
# cannot shorten the run. WER_ML_OUTPUT_DIR is not a default: the script's
# is the evaluation directory itself. The script is unchanged since
# 6f9bf56, but the module it runs, evaluation/benchmark_wer.py, has
# changed (f0ac4e3 added --device and --dtype), so a reproduction meant to
# match the original exactly runs from a checkout of 6f9bf56. That commit
# predates this file, so copy the file into the checkout's hpc/runs/ from
# a current clone first. At 6f9bf56 the environment record and the
# summaries' run_metadata ask git about tracked files only, so the
# untracked copy does not mark the run as modified.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), one submission per card
# type. Each command stops at "|| exit 1" when the recipe is missing.
# Without it, bash carries on past a "." that cannot find its file, and
# sbatch submits the script with its own defaults, which write into the
# evaluation directory itself.
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/fleurs_ml.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --array=0,3 --gres=gpu:h100:1 --constraint=nvlink \
#       hpc/submit_benchmark_wer_multilingual.sh )
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/fleurs_ml.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --array=1 --gres=gpu:a100:1 \
#       hpc/submit_benchmark_wer_multilingual.sh )
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/fleurs_ml.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --array=2,4,5 --gres=gpu:l40s:1 \
#       hpc/submit_benchmark_wer_multilingual.sh )
#
# A reproduction writes to its own directory under repro/, so it cannot
# overwrite the ARC copy of the original run it is to be compared with, and
# the script refuses to write a task's summary over an existing one unless
# OVERWRITE=1.
# original: WER_ML_OUTPUT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/fleurs_ml"
WER_ML_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3
WER_ML_CONDITIONS=raw,pipeline_full
WER_ML_LIMIT=
WER_ML_OUTPUT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/fleurs_ml"
